## open
small
  p Issue 18 · [Read on the web](https://allotment.example/18)
h1 Garlic, frost, and the seed swap
p Plant your garlic *before* the ground freezes. Most of us put it in late last year and still got a fair crop, but the bulbs were small.
p The **seed swap** is on Saturday the 28th at the hut. Bring labelled envelopes; [the list is here](https://allotment.example/swap).
h2 Frost dates
p Last year the first hard frost came on **4␣November**. This year the forecast says the 20th, which gives the late beans a little longer.
quote
  p “Cover the brassicas, not the leeks. Leeks laugh at frost.”
h3 From the shed
ul
  -
    p The water is off from 1 December.
  -
    p Two plots are free on the north side; ask at the hut.
hr
small
  p You get this letter because you joined the allotment society. [Leave the list](https://allotment.example/leave).
